findings.detail:
Many district and town pages appear to be one template with the place name swapped. Signs of this:
- slugs with a '-2' suffix (pogotowie-zamkowe.com.pl /slusarz-warszawa-wawer-2/), which suggests duplicate pages;
- street-level pages;
- the same phone number across many city domains;
- a Wawer page that just sends users back to the main site.

Google's spam policy defines doorway abuse as pages made to rank for similar queries that lead to less useful intermediate pages. Its examples include near-duplicate city pages, multiple lookalike domains for one business, and keyword-permutation pages. A page for a real location with real address, hours and unique content is not a doorway.

Our approach: no street pages, no microsites, no service × town matrix. Only a few town pages, each with genuinely local content, plus one canonical page per service.

Most locksmith 'pogotowie' sites treat car keys as one line. The car-key specialists (ImmoCODE Kraków, MobileKey Wrocław, Keylab, Chimko, kluczyki24.pl, mobilnymechanikwarszawa.eu, auto-klucze.com) are often dated .html sites or programmatic district pages.

Topics that a strong site covers:
- key types: plain blade, transponder with fixed vs. variable code, remote, keyless/smart key, Renault card;
- 'all keys lost' (utrata wszystkich kluczy) process: reading the profile from the lock or ignition, programming via the car's module;
- documents required: ID + registration certificate + VIN; 'no formalities' offers are a red flag;
- remote repair, ignition lock repair;
- mobile service: cut and code on site, drive away the same day;
- typical durations and price drivers.

The informational results are dominated by big portals (auto-swiat, otomoto, interia, link4, warta, noweopony, android.com.pl). A local business can win the long tail with Kielce-specific guides and a brand/model support list. Avoid publishing 'IMMO OFF' or immobilizer-removal offers, which appear in Kielce OLX ads. Present ECU/immobilizer work as legal repair, adaptation after module replacement and key programming, done with proof of ownership.
